# Optional: maps a share's mount point to the NetApp ONTAP SVM/volume
# that actually backs it, so restic-backup.sh can snapshot-then-backup
# that share instead of reading the live, changing filesystem
# directly (see "Backing up from a NetApp snapshot" in README.md for
# the full rationale and mechanism).
#
# One share per line: "<mount point>  <SVM name>  <volume name>".
# The SVM/volume names are ONTAP's own (System Manager, or `volume
# show -vserver <svm> -volume <volume>`) - they do NOT need to match
# the local mount point name or path.
#
# A share NOT listed here is backed up exactly as before (no NetApp
# snapshot involved) - this file is entirely opt-in, one share at a
# time. Copy to /etc/restic/netapp-volumes.conf; if that file doesn't
# exist at all, nothing here is required and every share just backs
# up directly as always.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.

/mnt/svm-cs3-bnl-dev/presentation_copy    svm-cs3-bnl-dev    presentation_copy_vol01
/mnt/SVMCIGOUVZ1001/test                  SVMCIGOUVZ1001     test_vol
